1
00:00:00,269 --> 00:00:02,229
(Sheldon:)The parade.

2
00:00:03,731 --> 00:00:06,821
(Penny:)That reminds me. I usually go back
to Nebraska for Thanksgiving.

3
00:00:06,984 --> 00:00:10,074
(Penny:)This year, they're calling it off
on account of my brother's trial.

4
00:00:10,237 --> 00:00:13,907
(Leonard:)-What's he on trial for?
-Oh, just a big misunderstanding.

5
00:00:14,075 --> 00:00:17,165
You know, you'd like my brother.
He's kind of a chemist.

6
00:00:20,164 --> 00:00:22,164
(Penny:)I was thinking
I'd have Thanksgiving here.

7
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:24,503
(Penny:)-And you are all invited.
-Oh, I'll be there.

8
00:00:24,668 --> 00:00:28,668
(Sheldon:)Will you be serving cranberry jelly
or cranberry sauce?

9
00:00:29,131 --> 00:00:30,461
(Penny:)I guess I could serve both.

10
00:00:30,633 --> 00:00:34,593
(Sheldon:)You guess? You don't seem
to have much of a handle on this.

11
00:00:35,638 --> 00:00:38,138
(Howard:)Yeah, I really wish I could,
Penny, but every year...

12
00:00:38,307 --> 00:00:43,307
(Howard:)...my mother has all the relatives over
and cooks up her famous tur-briska-fil.

13
00:00:43,979 --> 00:00:45,479
(Penny:)Tur-briska-fil?

14
00:00:45,773 --> 00:00:48,943
A turkey stuffed with a brisket
stuffed with gefilte fish.

15
00:00:50,903 --> 00:00:53,533
(Howard:)It's not as good as it sounds.

16
00:00:54,281 --> 00:00:55,611
(Penny:)Raj, what about you?

17
00:00:55,783 --> 00:00:57,533
(Howard:)Oh, he usually comes
to my house. Right, pal?

18
00:00:58,035 --> 00:00:59,785
[SOBS]

19
00:01:01,872 --> 00:01:05,872
Uh, all right. This year,
you don't have to eat the tur-briska-fil.

20
00:01:07,378 --> 00:01:12,018
(Howard:)I don't even chew it.
I swallow it like pills.

